{"content":[{"c":["FISHERMEN"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Those who caught fish for a living. Fishing was carried on by fishermen in the Holy Land from early times and is referred to in both the OT (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.19.8","r":"Isa.19.8","rawR":"Isa.19.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.19.8","value":"Isa.19.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 19:8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.16.16","r":"Jer.16.16","rawR":"Jer.16.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.16.16","value":"Jer.16.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 16:16"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.47.10","r":"Ezek.47.10","rawR":"Ezek.47.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.47.10","value":"Ezek.47.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 47:10"},") and the NT (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.4.18-19","r":"Matt.4.18-19","rawR":"Matt.4.18-19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.4.18-19","value":"Matt.4.18-19"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 4:18-19"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.1.16-17","r":"Mark.1.16-17","rawR":"Mark.1.16-17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.1.16-17","value":"Mark.1.16-17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mk 1:16-17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.5.2","r":"Luke.5.2","rawR":"Luke.5.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.5.2","value":"Luke.5.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 5:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=John.21.7","r":"John.21.7","rawR":"John.21.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.21.7","value":"John.21.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jn 21:7"},"). Fishermen formed a distinct class in society. Jesus included several fishermen among his disciples (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.4.18-22","r":"Matt.4.18-22","rawR":"Matt.4.18-22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.4.18-22","value":"Matt.4.18-22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 4:18-22"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.1.16-20","r":"Mark.1.16-20","rawR":"Mark.1.16-20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.1.16-20","value":"Mark.1.16-20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mk 1:16-20"},"; cf. ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.5.2-11","r":"Luke.5.2-11","rawR":"Luke.5.2-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.5.2-11","value":"Luke.5.2-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 5:2-11"},"). Their work was strenuous (",{"href":"?bref=Luke.5.2-5","r":"Luke.5.2-5","rawR":"Luke.5.2-5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.5.2-5","value":"Luke.5.2-5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 5:2-5"},") and not always rewarding (",{"href":"?bref=Luke.5.5","r":"Luke.5.5","rawR":"Luke.5.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.5.5","value":"Luke.5.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 5:5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=John.21.3","r":"John.21.3","rawR":"John.21.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.21.3","value":"John.21.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jn 21:3"},"). Jesus used the metaphor “fishers of men” of his disciples to denote how they would “catch” people for the kingdom (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.4.19","r":"Matt.4.19","rawR":"Matt.4.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.4.19","value":"Matt.4.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 4:19"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.1.17","r":"Mark.1.17","rawR":"Mark.1.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.1.17","value":"Mark.1.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mk 1:17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.5.10","r":"Luke.5.10","rawR":"Luke.5.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.5.10","value":"Luke.5.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 5:10"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Fishermen","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Is 19:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.19.8","rawQueryValue":"Isa.19.8","sourceRefExact":"Isa.19.8"},{"anchorText":"Jer 16:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.16.16","rawQueryValue":"Jer.16.16","sourceRefExact":"Jer.16.16"},{"anchorText":"Ez 47:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.47.10","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.47.10","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.47.10"},{"anchorText":"Mt 4:18-19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.4.18-19","rawQueryValue":"Matt.4.18-19","sourceRefExact":"Matt.4.18-19"},{"anchorText":"Mk 1:16-17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mark.1.16-17","rawQueryValue":"Mark.1.16-